    "label": "ORP: focus clamp off-by-one (OOB risk)",
    "expect": "SURVIVED",
    "why": "EQUIVALENT MUTANT \u2014 not a test gap, and no test can close it. bucket(s) <= s-1 for every s >= 1, and leadingPunct + strippedLength <= count, so orpIndex <= count-1 always; the clamp never fires and both forms behave identically. Proven analytically (pure counting, so character-set independent) and empirically over 1,411,111 words \u2014 exhaustive to length 6 over an adversarial alphabet plus 300k random to length 40 \u2014 with zero counterexamples and a tightest slack of exactly 0. The clamp stays as cheap insurance; the invariant that makes it dead is what a test should pin."
  },
